==English==

===Etymology===
From the magazine ''[[w:Billboard (magazine)|Billboard]]''<nowiki/>'s practice, in the 1960s and 1970s, of putting a [[bullet]] sign in front of chart entries for songs that had sold one million singles.

===Adjective===
{{en-adj|-|head=[[with]] a [[bullet]]}}

# {{context|of a hit record|lang=en}} that has entered the [[chart]]s in a high position, or has climbed rapidly in the charts, or is thought to have the [[potential]] for further rapid advancement
#: ''"Free The World" has moved up again and is now Number 25 '''with a bullet''' on the Billboard Hot Dance/Club Play Charts!!"''

